ecm_interface: fix the multicast hierarchy row bound

ecm_interface_multicast_heirarchy_construct_bridge_nonsrcdev() walks the
bridge slaves of a multicast destination and, for each, takes a hierarchy
row to build into:

	int total_if = valid_if + br_if;
	...
	if (total_if > ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX) {
		...
		goto fail2;
	}
	ifaces = ecm_db_multicast_if_heirarchy_get(interfaces, total_if);

total_if is an index, not a count, and the allocation behind interfaces is
exactly ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX rows -

	#define ECM_DB_TO_MCAST_INTERFACES_SIZE (sizeof(struct ecm_db_iface_instance *) \
			* ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX * ECM_DB_IFACE_HEIRARCHY_MAX)

- with no spare row, so a total_if of exactly 16 passes the test and
addresses one whole row (ECM_DB_IFACE_HEIRARCHY_MAX pointers) past the
end. The hierarchy is then constructed into it.

The same file already states the correct form for an index a few lines
down, DEBUG_ASSERT(valid_if < ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX). Note the two
sibling tests at the same bound are NOT the same defect and are left
alone: the one on if_num and the one on valid_if at the end of the
function both guard counts, where 16 is a legitimate full set, and
tightening them would reject a valid 16-way multicast group.

The accessor's own DEBUG_ASSERT(index <= ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX) is off
by one for the same reason, but it is left for now: with this call site
corrected, an index of 16 can no longer reach it from here, and
tightening a live assert - ECM builds at debug level 1, so DEBUG_ASSERT
is BUG() - without first auditing every other caller would convert a
latent condition into a panic on a path multicast traffic drives.
Recorded in OPEN-BUGS.md instead.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

--- a/ecm_interface.c
+++ b/ecm_interface.c
@@ -5417,7 +5417,7 @@ int32_t ecm_interface_multicast_heirarch
 					continue;
 				}
 
-				if (total_if > ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX) {
+				if (total_if >= ECM_DB_MULTICAST_IF_MAX) {
 					ecm_interface_hierarchy_delete(interfaces, interface_first_base, total_if);
 					dev_put(mc_br_slave_dev);
 					goto fail2;
